Fix for clingox UPSTREAM-ISSUES U46: the application's control never delivers
the statistics and finish events of a solve when clasp is built without threads.

ClingoApp::onEvent forwards clasp's StepReady event to ClingoControl::onFinish,
which delivers on_statistics and on_finish to the solve event handler
(clingo_solve_event_type_statistics and _finish), only inside
"#if CLASP_HAS_THREADS". ClingoLib::onEvent, the library control's twin, has no
such guard. Without threads (WebAssembly without atomics) a solve with a
handler on the control of clingo_main therefore gets its model and unsat events
but never the statistics and finish events, in any solve mode.

The call is safe to make in every build. The application's control passes no
event handler to ClaspFacade::solve, so StepReady reaches it only through
the shared context's handler, once per step (stopStep reports it under
"!solved()"), and onFinish clears the handler it delivered to. Threaded builds
already run exactly this code. Against clingo v5.8.2; suitable for upstream.

diff --git a/libclingo/src/clingo_app.cc b/libclingo/src/clingo_app.cc
--- a/libclingo/src/clingo_app.cc
+++ b/libclingo/src/clingo_app.cc
@@ -180,12 +180,10 @@
     return BaseType::onModel(s, m) && ret;
 }
 void ClingoApp::onEvent(Clasp::Event const &ev) {
-#if CLASP_HAS_THREADS
     Clasp::ClaspFacade::StepReady const *r = Clasp::event_cast<Clasp::ClaspFacade::StepReady>(ev);
     if (r && grd) {
         grd->onFinish(r->summary->result);
     }
-#endif
     BaseType::onEvent(ev);
 }
 void ClingoApp::run(Clasp::ClaspFacade &clasp) {
